"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nSince the main branch of Song Fa Bak Kut Teh is often crowded and described as less pleasant, I headed to this cleaner branch.  \n\nBeing located inside a mall, the interior was definitely comfortable and cool.  \nThere was a wait, but I was able to enter without waiting too long.  \n\nThe taste was familiar, similar to Korean Galbi-tang.  \nThe broth is a bit clearer and oilier than Galbi-tang, but the strong garlic and pepper notes made it very enjoyable.  \n\nThe soup is refillable, and rice must be ordered separately."